# python3 bin/python/brick_wall_castles.py  (2026-10-29, Python 3.11.12)
[1] the shear is a bijection from the brick-wall castles of width w onto the 1-histograms of width w, row t of the wall becoming row t of the histogram shifted t places, so height, blocks and cells agree; the mirror images drop by at most 1 and end at height 1; w <= 10: True
[2] the column sweep agrees with brute force on the walls by (height, blocks), w <= 10: True; by width C_w and by blocks N(w, k), w <= 16: True; by height the Dyck paths of semilength w and height h (A080936), w <= 16: True
[3] even-block brick-wall castles, w = 1..16: [0, 1, 3, 7, 20, 66, 217, 715, 2424, 8398, 29414, 104006, 371384, 1337220, 4847637, 17678835]; = A071688(w) (OEIS data, 2026-10-29): True; = C_w/2 (w even), (C_w + (-1)^((w+1)/2) C_((w-1)/2))/2 (w odd): True
[4] brick-wall castles by w + blocks, s = 2..16: [1, 1, 2, 4, 8, 17, 37, 82, 185, 423, 978, 2283, 5373, 12735, 30372]; = A004148(s - 1), the peakless Motzkin paths of length s - 1: True
[5] brick-wall castles by cells n = 0..18 (the empty wall at n = 0): [1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 9, 15, 26, 45, 78, 135, 234, 406, 704, 1222, 2120, 3679, 6385]; = A005169 (OEIS data): True; by (cells, width) = [x^n y^w] of 1/(1 - xy/(1 - x^2 y/(1 - x^3 y/ ...))), n <= 18: True
[6] sum (-1)^k q^(p C(k+1,2))/(q)_k / sum (-1)^k q^(k + p C(k,2))/(q)_k = 1 + the (p - 1)-histograms by area, p = 2, 3, 4, area <= 16: [True, True, True]; at p = 2, [1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 9, 15, 26, 45, 78, 135, 234]; at p = 1 the quotient is 1: True
[7] block fountains of width w = 1..14: [1, 2, 5, 13, 34, 89, 233, 610, 1597, 4181, 10946, 28657, 75025, 196418]; = the walls with one block per row, w <= 10: True; = F_(2w-1): True; = [y^w] (1 - 2y)/(1 - 3y + y^2): True; = sum_l C(w + l - 1, w - l - 1): True
[8] f_(w,s) = 1-histograms of width w with last column s agrees with Thomas and May's table, w <= 6: True; f_(w,s) = (s/w) C(2w - s - 1, w - s), w <= 8: True
[9] s_k = the level after the k-th up-step is a bijection from the Dyck paths of semilength w onto the 1-histograms of width w, with height = path height and blocks = w + 1 - peaks, w <= 12: True
[10] S_brick(w) = sum of (-1)^blocks, w = 1..16: [-1, 0, 1, 0, -2, 0, 5, 0, -14, 0, 42, 0, -132, 0, 429, 0]; = 0 (w even), (-1)^((w+1)/2) C_((w-1)/2) (w odd): True
[11] the Euler castles (falls of 0 or 1, last column 1), mirrored, are the sheared walls whose every row is one block ending at the right end of its row, 2^(w-1) of them, with strictly shorter rows going up, w <= 10: True
